  "worked_solution": "The sum (or difference) of two irrational numbers is *sometimes* rational and *sometimes* irrational. \n\nFor example:\n\n- $\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}=2.828\\,427\\,125…$ is irrational, yet\n\n- $\\sqrt{2}+(-\\sqrt{2})=0$ is rational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
